  "Question": "The radius of \\(\\odot O\\) is \\(5\\). Chord \\(AB\\parallel\\) chord \\(CD\\), \\(AB=6\\), and \\(CD=8\\). The two chords lie on opposite sides of the center \\(O\\). Find the distance between \\(AB\\) and \\(CD\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "7",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The distance from the center to \\(AB\\) is \\(\\sqrt{25-9}=4\\), and the distance from the center to \\(CD\\) is \\(\\sqrt{25-16}=3\\). Since the two chords lie on opposite sides of the center, the distance between them is \\(4+3=7\\).",
